Subject: [PATCH] S3: Full Swagger documentation for Stock & Cards modules
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Covers StockController, ProductItemsController, InventoryController
(batch upload), InventoryHistoryController, CardFilesController (13
endpoints).

- Add Swagger/Examples/StockExamples.cs, ProductItemExamples.cs,
  InventoryExamples.cs, InventoryHistoryExamples.cs,
  CardFileExamples.cs and register them in ExampleCatalog.
- Backfill missing <response> XML doc tags on all 13 actions.
- Continue the 401/403 accuracy audit: InventoryController.Upload and
  CardFilesController.Generate each have a rare enveloped-401 edge
  case (Batch.ActorNotResolved / CardFile.ActorNotResolved), same
  shape as Tenant.ActorNotResolved (S1) and Branch/Product's
  ActorNotResolved (S2).
- Document CardFilesController.Generate's 200 as non-JSON (the raw
  .dat file; hand-off metadata travels in X-File-Mac/X-Card-Count/
  X-Expected-Row-Count headers instead) — no 200 example is
  registered for it, same reasoning as PrintImagesController.Get's
  raw-bytes response from S2.
- Confirm via StockService that GetByBranch never 404s on an unknown
  branch (returns an empty page).
- Update Docs/PROJECT_KNOWLEDGE.md (§3, §18, metadata trailer) with
  S3 coverage and both new findings.

Remaining controllers land in S4 (Transactions/CardDisposals) and S5
(BranchRequests).
